.TH PACK 1 "April 2026" "pack-extract 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pack \- create compressed archives in the specified format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pack
.I format source
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pack
creates an archive or compressed file from the given
.I source
(file or directory) in the specified
.IR format .
The output is placed in the current directory, named after the source
with the appropriate extension appended.
.PP
This avoids having to remember tool-specific flags for each format.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.SS Archive formats (files and directories)
.TS
l l l.
Format	Extension	Tool used
_
tar	.tar	tar
tar.gz	.tar.gz	tar + gzip
tar.xz	.tar.xz	tar + xz
tar.bz2	.tar.bz2	tar + bzip2
tar.zst	.tar.zst	tar \-\-zstd
tar.lz4	.tar.lz4	tar + lz4
tar.lz	.tar.lz	tar \-\-lzip
zip	.zip	zip
7z	.7z	7z
.TE
.SS Single-file compression (files only)
.TS
l l l.
Format	Extension	Tool used
_
gz	.gz	gzip
bz2	.bz2	bzip2
xz	.xz	xz
zstd	.zst	zstd
lz4	.lz4	lz4
.TE
.PP
Single-file formats (gz, bz2, xz, zstd, lz4) refuse to operate on
directories. Use an archive format instead.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a gzip-compressed tarball of a directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pack tar.gz project/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a zip archive:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pack zip src/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a 7z archive:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pack 7z backups/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a zstd-compressed tarball:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pack tar.zst dataset/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compress a single file with gzip:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pack gz report.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Archive created successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (source not found, unsupported format, directory with
single-file format, creation failure).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B pack
relies on standard system utilities. Not all need to be installed;
only those for the formats you use:
.BR tar (1),
.BR gzip (1),
.BR bzip2 (1),
.BR xz (1),
.BR zstd (1),
.BR lz4 (1),
.BR zip (1),
.BR 7z (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR extract (1),
.BR tar (1),
.BR gzip (1),
.BR zip (1),
.BR 7z (1)
